--- body ---
## Author mandate (2026-10-14)

Refactor the articulation AND names of the review workflow. Current overlap:
raid orchestrates tickets; hunt already runs review-pr; gaze orchestrates
another review battery, including review-pr; review-pr itself orchestrates
reviewers. PR-based naming (review-pr) also clashes with content-based naming
(review-pr-prose, called review-prose in discussion).

The author requests this follow-up after raids 1080/1089 exceeded the requested
20-minute closing window. Implementation belongs to a later session. Related
resource-lifecycle discussion is deferred separately under 1095.

## Required direction

Hunt owns a justified, proportionate review plan based on risk and actual
review history. The plan controls execution, rather than merely narrating it:
what valid evidence exists, what changed since it, which perspectives remain
necessary, why and at what budget. Reuse valid current evidence; no automatic
second battery for an unchanged diff.

The review / review-code / review-prose arrangement is a candidate, not an
approved three-skill architecture. The author explicitly reserves judgment
on that extra layer. Compare a single review skill with content-specific modes
against separate helpers, and justify the smallest arrangement that meets the
needs. Hunt controls the chosen review mechanism. Preserve useful standalone
review invocation. Raid coordinates tickets and merges, not a second per-ticket
review orchestrator. Remove gaze as a separate orchestration layer, or retain
only a compatibility alias that does not add another battery.

Keep verify-gate as the final check of actual exit criteria, comments and
applicable proof for the final head/base. Reviewers remain distinct from the
coder; required lineage independence and actual identity/coverage records
still apply. Missing review evidence must never become simulated approval.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Hunt produces and executes the justified review plan above, with explicit
      reuse/invalidation decisions tied to revisions and affected scope.
- [ ] Resolve the author's reservation about a three-skill architecture: compare
      simpler alternatives and justify the chosen names and responsibilities;
      gaze removal or compatibility-only behavior is explicit.
- [ ] verify-gate still blocks missing criteria, unresolved blocking findings
      and absent required proof; merge remains a separate caller decision.
- [ ] Regression scenarios demonstrate unchanged-head reuse without duplicate
      reviewers, proportionate re-review after relevant changes, and rejection
      of stale/missing proof. They test behavior, not wording alone.
- [ ] Update affected skills, profiles, callers, documentation and catalog;
      split into child PRs before implementation if the 15-file breaker applies,
      and verify their integration before closing the tracker.

